.\" Man page for img2svg in roff/groff format.
.\" Compatible with groff (Linux), mandoc (FreeBSD), and the BSD mdoc(7)
.\" toolchain's roff compatibility mode.
.TH IMG2SVG 1 "2026-06-10" "0.1.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
img2svg \- convert raster images to SVG with object and pattern detection

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B img2svg
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIINPUT\fR [\-o \fIOUTPUT\fR]
.PP
.B img2svg list-gpus
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B img2svg info

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B img2svg
converts raster images (PNG, JPEG, BMP, WebP, TIFF, GIF) into clean,
optimized SVG files.
It uses YOLO (via
.B ultralytics
) to detect and segment distinct objects, then
.B vtracer
to vectorize the remaining background.
Each conversion produces an
.I .svg
file and a matching
.I .json
sidecar containing detection metadata, classification, timing, and
a SHA-256 of the output.
.PP
The default invocation (\fBimg2svg \fIINPUT\fR) treats \fIINPUT\fR as
a single file path, a glob pattern, or a directory of images.
When \fIINPUT\fR is a directory, every supported image inside is
converted in batch.
When \fIINPUT\fR contains glob metacharacters
.RB ( * ? [ ),
the shell-expanded matches are processed as a batch.
.PP
The output mode controls how the detected regions and the background
are rendered; see
.B "OUTPUT MODES"
below.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR
Output file (single-file mode) or output directory (batch mode).
Required for single-file conversion.
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIMODE\fR
Output rendering mode.
One of:
.BR auto ,
.BR labels ,
.BR visual ,
.BR annotated ,
.BR trace ,
.BR poster ,
.BR detailed ,
.BR edge ,
.BR watercolor ,
.BR segmented .
Defaults to
.BR auto .
See
.B "OUTPUT MODES"
for details.
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fINAME\fR
YOLO model file or Ultralytics hub name.
Defaults to
.BR yolo11x.pt .
The model is downloaded on first use and cached under
.BR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/img2svg/models/ .
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fIDEVICE\fR
Compute device selector.
One of:
.BR auto ,
.BR cpu ,
.BR cuda ,
.BR cuda: N
.RB (specific CUDA device),
.BR mps
(Apple Silicon),
.BR rocm
(AMD).
Defaults to
.BR auto .
.TP
\fB\-\-gpu\-strategy\fR \fISTRATEGY\fR
GPU recommendation strategy used when \fB\-\-device\fR is
.BR auto .
One of:
.BR auto ,
.BR power
(pick the GPU with the most free VRAM),
.BR availability
(pick the first free device).
.TP
\fB\-\-conf\fR \fIFLOAT\fR
YOLO confidence threshold, in
.BR [0.0, 1.0] .
Detections below this score are discarded.
Defaults to
.BR 0.25 .
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-clobber\fR
Do not overwrite an existing output file.
If the target \fI.svg\fR already exists, the input is skipped and
the batch continues with the next file.
.TP
\fB\-\-preprocess\fR \fIFILTER\fR
Preprocessing filter to apply before tracing.
May be repeated to chain multiple filters in order.
One of:
.BR bilateral
(edge-preserving denoise),
.BR nlmeans
(non-local means denoise),
.BR median
(median denoise),
.BR unsharp
(unsharp mask sharpening).
Overridden by
.BR \-\-no\-preprocess .
.TP
\fB\-\-denoise\fR \fIFILTER\fR
Convenience shortcut for a single denoise filter.
One of:
.BR bilateral ,
.BR nlmeans ,
.BR median ,
or empty to disable.
Equivalent to
.B \-\-preprocess \fIFILTER\fR
when non-empty.
.TP
\fB\-\-sharpen\fR \fIFILTER\fR
Convenience shortcut for a single sharpen filter.
One of:
.BR unsharp ,
or empty to disable.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-colors\fR \fIINT\fR
Maximum number of distinct colors in the output
.RB ( 0
means no cap, the default).
Valid range:
.BR 2 \- 256
when non-zero.
.TP
\fB\-\-quality\fR \fIINT\fR
JPEG-style quality hint stored in the sidecar for reproducibility
.RB ( 1 \- 100 ,
default
.BR 90 ).
Does not affect the SVG output.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-preprocess\fR
Disable all preprocessing, overriding any
.B \-\-preprocess ,
.B \-\-denoise ,
or
.B \-\-sharpen
choices.
.TP
\fB\-\-seg\-model\fR \fINAME\fR
YOLO segmentation model variant.
One of:
.BR yolo11n\-seg ,
.BR yolo11s\-seg ,
.BR yolo11m\-seg ,
.BR yolo11l\-seg ,
.BR yolo11x\-seg .
Defaults to
.BR yolo11s\-seg .
Used by
.B \-\-mode segmented
and by any other segmentation-aware pipeline stage.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-seg\fR
Disable segmentation even when the active mode would normally
invoke the segmentor.
The
.B segmented
mode falls back to a single whole-image trace (same as
.BR visual )
when this flag is set.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-svg\-size\fR \fIMB\fR
Hard upper bound on the rendered SVG's on-disk size in MB.
If the output exceeds this cap, the file is deleted and the run
fails.
Valid range:
.BR 1 \- 1024 .
Defaults to
.BR 50 .
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non-essential output (progress bars, status lines).
Errors are still printed to stderr.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable debug-level logging to stderr.
.TP
\fB\-\-preprocess\fR \fIFILTER\fR
Preprocessing filter to apply before tracing.
May be repeated.
Filters: bilateral, nlmeans, median, unsharp.
Overridden by
.B \-\-no\-preprocess
\&.
.TP
\fB\-\-denoise\fR \fIFILTER\fR
Denoise filter: bilateral, nlmeans, median, or empty to disable.
.TP
\fB\-\-sharpen\fR \fIFILTER\fR
Sharpen filter: unsharp, or empty to disable.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-colors\fR \fIINT\fR
Max distinct colors in the output (0 = no cap, 2-256).
.TP
\fB\-\-quality\fR \fIINT\fR
JPEG quality hint stored in the sidecar (1-100).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-preprocess\fR
Disable all preprocessing, overriding any
.B \-\-preprocess
choices.
.TP
\fB\-\-seg\-model\fR \fINAME\fR
YOLO segmentation model variant.
One of: yolo11n-seg, yolo11s-seg, yolo11m-seg, yolo11l-seg, yolo11x-seg.
Used by the
.B segmented
mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-seg\fR
Disable segmentation even when the active mode would normally use it.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-svg\-size\fR \fIINT\fR
Hard upper bound on the rendered SVG's on-disk size in MB.
If the output exceeds this cap, the file is deleted and the run fails.
Range: 1-1024. Default: 50.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the
.B img2svg
version and exit 0.
.TP
\fBlist\-gpus\fR \fB\-\-strategy\fR \fISTRATEGY\fR
Subcommand: list detected GPUs and the recommended one for the
given strategy. Exits 0 even when no GPU is found.
.TP
\fBinfo\fR
Subcommand: print version, Python version, OS, and detected compute
devices. Useful for bug reports.

.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a single PNG to SVG (auto mode):
.PP
.EX
img2svg photo.png \-o photo.svg
.EE
.PP
Convert every supported image in a directory (batch mode):
.PP
.EX
img2svg photos/ \-o svgs/
.EE
.PP
Process a glob pattern:
.PP
.EX
img2svg "*.jpg" \-o svgs/
.EE
.PP
Force a specific output mode (bounding boxes + labels, useful for
diagrams and screenshots):
.PP
.EX
img2svg diagram.png \-o diagram.svg \-\-mode labels
.EE
.PP
Use the high-fidelity photo trace (the
.B auto
default for photos):
.PP
.EX
img2svg photo.jpg \-o photo.svg \-\-mode detailed
.EE
.PP
Chain a denoise and a sharpen filter before tracing:
.PP
.EX
img2svg photo.jpg \-o photo.svg \-\-mode detailed \-\-denoise bilateral \-\-sharpen unsharp
.EE
.PP
Produce a multi-layer editable SVG with one group per detected
object (uses the default
.B yolo11s\-seg
segmentation model):
.PP
.EX
img2svg group.jpg \-o group.svg \-\-mode segmented \-\-seg\-model yolo11s\-seg
.EE
.PP
Pin a specific CUDA device:
.PP
.EX
img2svg photo.png \-o out.svg \-\-device cuda:0
.EE
.PP
List detected GPUs with the default recommendation strategy:
.PP
.EX
img2svg list\-gpus
.EE
.PP
Print runtime environment for a bug report:
.PP
.EX
img2svg info
.EE

.SH "OUTPUT MODES"
.TP
.B auto
Inspect the input with a heuristic classifier (alpha, edge density,
color count) and pick a mode automatically.
Logos, diagrams, screenshots, and line art become
.BR visual ;
photographs become
.BR detailed .
.BR labels
and
.BR annotated
are explicit-only and never picked automatically.
.TP
.B labels
Render only the YOLO detections: bounding boxes with class labels
and confidence. Useful for QA and dataset inspection. No background
is vectorized.
.TP
.B visual
Run
.B vtracer
across the full image with the default color preset, preserving
gradients, shadows, and color regions. Detections are not drawn.
.TP
.B annotated
Combine
.B visual
and
.BR labels :
vtracer output is the background, with detection boxes and labels
overlaid on top.
.TP
.B trace
Run
.B vtracer
with the binary (binary=1) / line-art preset: thinner outlines, no
color clusters, optimized for black-and-white line art and icons.
.TP
.B poster
Run
.B vtracer
with the
.B poster
preset: flat color regions, lower color precision, suitable for
screen-print and marketing-poster aesthetics.
.TP
.B detailed
Run
.B vtracer
with the
.B photo_hifi
preset: high color precision, tight layer difference, more
iterations, and a higher path precision than
.BR visual .
The
.B auto
default for photographs.
.TP
.B edge
Run
.B vtracer
in polygon mode with binary color and a high corner threshold.
Produces line-art output. Pairs well with
.B \-\-preprocess median
on scanned line art or product silhouettes.
.TP
.B watercolor
Run
.B vtracer
with the
.B watercolor
preset: soft painterly output with a low corner threshold, larger
splines, and a high
.BR filter_speckle .
.TP
.B segmented
Run YOLO instance segmentation on the input. Each detected object
is traced with
.B vtracer "'s" \fBphoto_hifi\fR
preset and emitted as its own
.B <g>
group
.RB ( \fBid="obj_\fIclass\fR_\fIidx\fB"\fR )
in the output SVG. The background is traced separately and emitted
as
.BR <g id="background" data-role="background"> .
Requires
.B \-\-seg\-model
and benefits from a CUDA or MPS device for the YOLO inference.
See the
.B PHOTO MODES
section below for the deep dive.

.SH "PHOTO MODES"
The five photo modes
.RB ( \fBposter\fR ,
.BR detailed ,
.BR edge ,
.BR watercolor ,
.BR segmented )
share a common pipeline. By default the image is fed to the
renderer as-is. The optional preprocessing chain runs first when
enabled.
.PP
\fBPreprocessing.\fR
.B \-\-preprocess
takes a filter name
.RB ( bilateral ,
.BR nlmeans ,
.BR median ,
.BR unsharp )
and may be repeated to chain multiple filters. The
.B \-\-denoise
and
.B \-\-sharpen
flags are convenience shortcuts for the most common single-filter
chains. All preprocessing is disabled by
.B \-\-no\-preprocess ,
which overrides any positive choices.
.PP
\fBSegmentation.\fR
.B \-\-mode segmented
invokes a YOLO segmentation model
(selected by
.B \-\-seg\-model
and defaulting to
.BR yolo11s\-seg )
to detect objects. Each object's mask is traced with
.B vtracer "'s" \fBphoto_hifi\fR
preset, and the result is grouped by class in the output SVG.
.B \-\-no\-seg
disables segmentation even when
.B segmented
mode is active; the renderer falls back to a single whole-image
trace (same as
.BR visual ).
The available models are
.BR yolo11n\-seg ,
.BR yolo11s\-seg ,
.BR yolo11m\-seg ,
.BR yolo11l\-seg ,
and
.BR yolo11x\-seg .
Smaller models are faster; larger models are more accurate.
.BR yolo11x\-seg
requires a discrete GPU with at least 6 GB of VRAM.
.PP
\fBColor cap.\fR
.B \-\-max\-colors
caps the number of distinct colors in the output SVG. The range
is
.B 0
(no cap, the default) to
.BR 256 .
Use a small value like
.B 8
to force a posterized look.
.PP
\fBOutput size cap.\fR
.B \-\-max\-svg\-size
sets a hard upper bound (in MB) on the rendered SVG's on-disk size.
If the output exceeds the cap, the file is deleted and the run
fails. The range is
.B 1
to
.B 1024
MB; the default is
.BR 50 .
Useful for catching runaway traces on large images.

.SH "GPU SUPPORT"
By default (\fB\-\-device auto\fR)
.B img2svg
autodetects the best available compute device at startup.
On Linux, NVIDIA GPUs are enumerated via
.BR nvidia\-smi
and AMD GPUs via
.BR rocm\-smi .
On macOS, the Apple MPS backend is selected when available.
On any host with no usable accelerator, \fBimg2svg\fR falls back to
\fBcpu\fR transparently.
.PP
Multi-vendor setups (NVIDIA + AMD on the same host) are supported.
The \fB\-\-gpu\-strategy\fR flag controls which device is picked:
.B power
selects the GPU with the most free VRAM,
.B availability
selects the first device with free VRAM, and
.B auto
lets
.B img2svg
choose.
.PP
To force a specific device regardless of autodetection, pass it
explicitly:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
img2svg photo.png \-o out.svg \-\-device cpu
img2svg photo.png \-o out.svg \-\-device cuda:0
img2svg photo.png \-o out.svg \-\-device mps
img2svg photo.png \-o out.svg \-\-device rocm
.EE
.RE

.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
For batch jobs, every input converted without error.
.TP
.B 1
Partial failure.
Batch mode completed, but at least one input failed
.I after
a successful pre-flight check.
General runtime failure for a single-file conversion.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid invocation.
Bad argument value (unknown mode, unknown strategy), unsupported
input format, missing input file, or output path collision.
.TP
.B 3
Dependency or model load failure.
The YOLO model could not be downloaded, torch failed to load, or
a required native library is missing.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/img2svg/
User-level configuration directory.
Honored
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when set.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/img2svg/
User-level data directory (output sidecars, presets).
Honored
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME
when set.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/img2svg/models/
Cached YOLO model weights.
Honored
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME
when set.
The active YOLO file is named after the \fB\-\-model\fR value
(e.g.\&
.BR yolo11x.pt ).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides
.I ~/.config
for configuration lookups.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Overrides
.I ~/.local/share
for data files.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Overrides
.I ~/.cache
for cached model weights.
.TP
.B CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES
Restricts the set of NVIDIA GPUs visible to
.B img2svg
(standard CUDA mechanism; respected by
\fB\-\-device\fR cuda
and the auto-detect path).

